  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A long straight wire of circular cross-section (radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>) is carrying steady current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is uniformly distributed across this cross-section. The magnetic field is</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "6NKis",
      "text": "<p>inversely&nbsp;proportional to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;region <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and uniform throughout in the region&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HgBAO",
      "text": "<p>directly proportional to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;in the region&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and inversely proportional to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;in the region&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jEY6m",
      "text": "Zero in the region&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and inversely proportional to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;in the region&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>a</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "t8vrS",
      "text": "<p>uniform in the region&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and inversely proportional to distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;from the axis, in the region&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the magnetic field inside the conducting wire is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>in&#160;</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>J</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>The formula to calculate the magnetic field outside the conducting wire is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>out&#160;</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>J</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>From equation (1), it can be concluded that the magnetic field is directly proportional to the&nbsp;radial distance inside the wire, whereas from equation (2), it can be concluded that the magnetic field is inversely proportional to the&nbsp;radial distance outside the wire.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
